 [OC]|cffffcc00Professions (Forever):|r recommended |cff66ff66Skinning + Leatherworking|r (Icy Veins' pick for Enhancement too), plus First Aid + Cooking. Why: Forever's new Leatherworking leveling sets - Totemic Leather (Str/Sta/Int + spell power) and Brawler's Leather (Str/Agi/Sta) - cover belt 12, gloves + chest 15, boots 17, legs + head 20, and beat the quest/dungeon pieces in this guide slot for slot; the patterns cost 30 Merchant's Favor each at the merchant camp on the Redridge border (chapter 18-19), and Leatherworking makes mail for you from 40. Passives: Skinning = +5% damage to Beasts and Dragonkin (stacks with Big Game Hunter), Leatherworking = +5% mount speed at max skill, Cooking = every cooked food gives a stat buff and an XP trickle, First Aid now makes the healing potions (Alchemy no longer does). Mining (+5% total health, ore money) is the alternative if you would rather not craft. Junior Mining/Skinning trainers stand in Anvilmar, so you can gather from level 2; Leatherworking is taught in Ironforge at 12.
 [OC][A Hunter] |cffffcc00Professions (Hunter):|r same answer - Skinning + Leatherworking. Brawler's Leather (Str/Agi/Sta) is your levelling set (skip the Totemic pieces), and Skinning's +5% vs Beasts stacks with Big Game Hunter. Cooking matters twice for you: your own food buff and cheap pet food (boars and bears eat bread, cheese, fish, fruit, fungus and meat).
 [OC]|cffffcc00Camping (Forever):|r Cooking 1 teaches the Basic Campfire (3 object slots). Sit or craft at a fire for 1 minute to get its buffs (1 hour). Each player adds ONE profession object: your Lodestone (Mining 20) = melee attack power, your Camp Chair (Skinning 20) = +2% crit, First Aid Kit = stamina, Fish Bowl = +8% all stats, Leatherworking tent = rested XP. Objects have a 1-hour cooldown and the fire vanishes after ~10-15 min, so set camp right before a dungeon or a long grind, with your friend adding his object. The Camping 101 quests (level 6, Eric Brighthammer) teach the tier-1 objects once that skill is 20.
+[OC]|cffffcc00Launch rule (1-6):|r no shared tags in Forever - on a camped named mob (Grik'nir, the Snow Leopard Prowler) INVITE the people standing there (kill credit shares in a party; most drop items don't). If no group forms in ~2 min, tick the step and keep moving; the catch-up line at the tunnel brings you back. Expect the first 10-20 min to be the worst: in 2019 the Coldridge crowd thinned 10-20 minutes after the first wave reached Grik'nir.
 
